Main goal: a target named __main__ is the default goal when the makefile named none
itself. Make still fills .DEFAULT_GOAL from the first rule as it reads, and remembers
that pick; when no goal is on the command line, a __main__ target replaces the pick, but
not a value a makefile or the AMK_GOAL knob assigned. Both places that read the default
settle it first: the ordinary run and a zygote request that names no goal.

